1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,980
First up, here are
supplemental funds for Sebas.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,900
Next, here is the reconstruction
assistance and equipment fund

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:11,240
for the Lizard Man villages.

4
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:14,030
That leaves...

5
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,710
That's all there is?!

6
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:22,370
It's not enough.
There's nowhere near enough money!

7
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:26,720
I wonder if it would be best
to get some merchant to sponsor me.

8
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:31,130
No, I have to avoid the impression
that the adventurer Momon

9
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:33,040
is only in it for the money.

10
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:37,360
Still, I really need the cash...

11
00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:40,970
Enter.

12
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:43,540
Is something wrong, Nabe?

13
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:48,310
Yes, Mr. Momon...

14
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,650
She's still doing it off and on--

15
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:53,780
it has become what I can
only describe as a verbal tic.

16
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:54,820
Well?

17
00:00:54,820 --> 00:01:01,160
Right. The iron ore that you ordered
from that merchant is ready.

18
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:03,950
I see. I'll get his payment ready at once.

19
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:11,630
But why are you ordering it
from so many different sources?

20
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:17,300
It's an experiment. I'm learning
how the Exchange Box appraises things.

21
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:21,060
Understood. Then I shall go buy it at once.

22
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:25,960
Right. And if the situation arises...
you know what to do, right?

23
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:29,650
I will give safety top priority,
and withdraw with all haste.

24
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:34,860
I will relocate to the counterfeit Nazarick
that Lord Aura is building,

25
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:37,570
thereby feeding false information
to the other side.

26
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:40,570
Very good. By no means
take any routes with large crowds,

27
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:43,410
where you may be easily attacked. And even
if you do get bumped by someone,

28
00:01:43,410 --> 00:01:46,710
or someone calls out to you,
do not grievously injure them.

29
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:48,460
No showering your bloodlust about, either.

30
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:51,590
And absolutely no calling humans "worms."

31
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:54,150
After all, we are Momon and Nabe,

32
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,720
hailed as high-ranking
raven black adventurers.

33
00:01:57,050 --> 00:01:57,970
Right.

34
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:00,440
Hmm. Okay, off you go, Nabe.

35
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:01,730
Right.

36
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:12,570
Ugh... Expenses always come
when you're out of money, huh?

37
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,400
Why don't you call it a day?

38
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:02,010
Lord Stronoff...

39
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:05,010
There's no point in overdoing it, Climb.

40
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,260
You are quite right.

41
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:08,760
My word,

42
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,520
if you really believe that,

43
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:15,730
I wish you wouldn't make me
repeat myself over and over again.

44
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:17,520
I am terribly sorry.

45
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:22,150
What do you say to a little practice match?

46
00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:24,070
But, sir...

47
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:28,450
Just recently, I was shown how callow I am.

48
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:31,330
I'd like to train with someone
who has a little resilience.

49
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:33,690
Who, <i>you</i>, Lord Stronoff?

50
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:38,670
Yeah. If a merciful magic caster
hadn't come to my aid,

51
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:41,920
I probably wouldn't
be standing here right now.

52
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:44,750
Who is this magic caster?

53
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,930
Ains Ooal Gown--

54
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:50,510
someone who, most likely,

55
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:52,730
could give that freakish wizard
from the Baharuth Empire

56
00:04:52,730 --> 00:04:54,560
a run for his money.

57
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:57,900
At least, that's what I think of him.

58
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:01,320
I will commit the gentleman's name to memory.

59
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:05,820
So then, are you sure you wish to train me?

60
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:08,760
Not training, just practicing 
with our swords.

61
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:12,490
Whether or not you take
anything away from it is up to you.

62
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:17,330
Now, come at me like this is actual combat.

63
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:23,020
Aren't you going?

64
00:05:24,130 --> 00:05:27,550
If not, I'll take the fight... to you!

65
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:37,900
Just because a sword is all I'm carrying

66
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:40,650
doesn't mean you should
focus all your attention on <i>it</i>.

67
00:05:40,650 --> 00:05:43,230
Otherwise, you could
get kicked like you just did.

68
00:05:43,650 --> 00:05:44,740
Right.

69
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:46,360
Ho...

70
00:05:47,030 --> 00:05:50,700
A typical soldier would be
finished after one of those.

71
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:53,740
I have to become stronger than I am.

72
00:05:54,450 --> 00:05:56,870
So I can keep Princess Renner safe.

73
00:05:57,250 --> 00:05:59,640
Mm-hmm. Bring it on, Climb!

74
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:10,470
Unfortunately for you, this will end up
the same way as last time...!

75
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:13,560
Martial Art! Fortress!

76
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,770
You were waiting for that?!

77
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:15,770
Yes!

78
00:06:17,390 --> 00:06:18,190
Martial Art!

79
00:06:18,690 --> 00:06:20,190
Slash!

80
00:06:27,610 --> 00:06:31,870
Bravo. Now I'm going to
take this a bit more seriously.

81
00:06:31,870 --> 00:06:33,370
Please do!

82
00:06:41,630 --> 00:06:42,530
How about it?

83
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:47,450
I was trying not to smash or
fracture anything while swinging at you.

84
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:52,890
Nothing worse than a bruise...
No problem at all...

85
00:06:52,890 --> 00:06:55,890
You'll be heading off
to bodyguard the princess now, right?

86
00:06:55,890 --> 00:06:56,770
Yes, sir...

87
00:06:56,770 --> 00:06:59,270
In that case, I'll give this to you.

88
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:02,220
Thank you very much.

89
00:07:03,770 --> 00:07:07,440
You really are amazing. How did you...

90
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:12,610
If you're asking how I got so strong,
I don't have a good answer.

91
00:07:12,610 --> 00:07:15,930
I simply happen to have a talent for it.

92
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:21,870
However, Climb, you're cut out
for the kind of fighting I do.

93
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:23,630
I... am?

94
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:26,880
Yeah. Those who receive formal training...

95
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:30,470
...can't help but focus
on fighting with their swords,

96
00:07:30,470 --> 00:07:32,770
but I don't see that as a good thing.

97
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:36,640
Realizing that the sword
is just one means of attacking,

98
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:39,390
and using your hands and feet
in your method of fighting

99
00:07:39,390 --> 00:07:41,140
are what will really be 
of use to you in combat.

100
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:44,900
Of course, that's more a style
for mud-ridden adventurers.

101
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:51,150
Thank you for your
pointers today, Lord Stronoff.

102
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:54,620
That strike from above was a pretty good one.

103
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:59,160
Although, you should also think about
what you're going to do next.

104
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,910
Right! I will!

105
00:08:00,910 --> 00:08:02,370
Head Warrior...

106
00:08:02,370 --> 00:08:03,460
Well, if you will excuse me...

107
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:04,940
What is it, Vice-Chief?

108
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:12,550
This is bad, sir.
He's Princess Renner's bodyguard.

109
00:08:12,550 --> 00:08:16,350
If word gets out that he fought the
royal head warrior, and either of you lost,

110
00:08:16,350 --> 00:08:18,970
the Noble Faction will have a field day.

111
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:22,560
I just wanted to fight someone
who could fight me back for a bit.

112
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:26,560
Well, I don't think anyone saw you.

113
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:29,190
He's an orphan whom
the princess took in on a whim.

114
00:08:29,190 --> 00:08:32,530
The nobles' antipathy
toward him is pretty strong,

115
00:08:32,530 --> 00:08:35,490
with him being a boy
from God only knows where.

116
00:08:35,490 --> 00:08:38,320
So, does he show
any promise for improvement?

117
00:08:38,830 --> 00:08:42,250
Nope. No matter how hard he tries,

118
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:45,570
he's what adventurers
would call "capped at gold."

119
00:08:46,170 --> 00:08:50,710
But while he may be limited by his ability,
he isn't limited by experience.

120
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:52,440
That's what I think.

121
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:54,720
That's...

122
00:08:55,090 --> 00:08:58,100
Prince Zanac and Marquis Raeven, isn't it?

123
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:01,360
Why would Marquis Raeven
of the Noble Faction be with him?

124
00:09:01,810 --> 00:09:04,140
Could he be switching sides
to the Royal Faction?

125
00:09:04,770 --> 00:09:07,730
It wouldn't surprise me
to see Marquis Raeven anywhere.

126
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,480
The man is an opportunist by nature.

127
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:13,290
He likely has many things
in motion behind the scenes.

128
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:33,510
Oh my, Climb. On your way
to visit that monster, are you?

129
00:09:34,170 --> 00:09:37,090
Your Highness, with all due respect,
Princess Renner is a person

130
00:09:37,090 --> 00:09:40,890
who could be called a kindhearted,
beautiful treasure of the kingdom.

131
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:45,270
<i>I</i> wasn't the one here who
just referred to Renner as a monster.

132
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:50,690
But a treasure?
Erecting facilities for the commoners,

133
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:55,690
and prohibiting transit tariffs
for adventurers? It's unheard-of.

134
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:59,200
Your Highness, I believe the measure
that abolished slave trafficking

135
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:02,280
that was passed the other day
was proposed by Princess Renner.

136
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:05,490
A rare exception.
But what about other than that?

137
00:10:06,250 --> 00:10:09,210
I have the feeling that she is
acting with the understanding

138
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:11,000
that what she is doing is impossible.

139
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,670
I am certain that she would not do so!

140
00:10:13,670 --> 00:10:17,880
I see, I see, then would you
tell that monster something for me?

141
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:21,760
Our elder brother, Barbro,
thinks of her as a political instrument,

142
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:24,140
but if she will work with 
me, the second prince,

143
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:25,770
he will relieve her of the title of princess,

144
00:10:25,770 --> 00:10:28,560
and grant her some territory
out on the frontiers.

145
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:33,440
Surely you jest!
I will pretend I did not hear that.

146
00:10:34,690 --> 00:10:35,940
That's a shame.

147
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:41,070
Ah, I almost forgot.

148
00:10:41,450 --> 00:10:43,240
Marquis Raeven is of the same opinion as me,

149
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:45,830
and says he considers that 
girl to be a monster.

150
00:10:45,830 --> 00:10:48,370
And since we see eye-to-eye,

151
00:10:48,370 --> 00:10:51,080
it seems that our joining forces
was the right call.

152
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,330
Prince Zanac...

153
00:10:52,630 --> 00:10:55,550
Don't worry about it, Marquis Raeven.
Knowing that monster,

154
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:58,770
I'm sure she already knows our opinion.

155
00:11:03,050 --> 00:11:05,760
Goodness, what is a commoner doing in here?

156
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,930
The princess is quite the fanciful one.

157
00:11:07,930 --> 00:11:09,100
Definitely.

158
00:11:12,730 --> 00:11:13,610
Pardon me.

159
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:18,000
Morning, Climb.

160
00:11:22,410 --> 00:11:26,340
Good morning,
Princess Renner... Lady Aindra....

161
00:11:26,910 --> 00:11:27,660
Whoops...

162
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:31,040
Oh, she's one of my team members.

163
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,290
This is Tina.

164
00:11:33,290 --> 00:11:38,050
I beg your pardon. It is a pleasure
to meet you. My name is Climb.

165
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:40,920
I am extremely pleased
to meet the renowned Lady Tina,

166
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:43,680
of the adventurers group Blue Rose.

167
00:11:45,050 --> 00:11:48,310
The pleasure's mine.
Thanks for looking out for our fiendish boss.

168
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:52,310
Climb, why don't you have a seat
before we start talking?

169
00:11:52,310 --> 00:11:54,660
But I am your bodyguard, so...

170
00:11:55,310 --> 00:11:57,070
It makes no difference to me.

171
00:11:57,070 --> 00:11:59,820
Yes, but... Lady Aindra...

172
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:02,700
I told you before, call me Lakyus.

173
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,950
Because you're so special, Climb.

174
00:12:04,950 --> 00:12:07,740
--Oof...
--Please don't joke like that.

175
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:09,450
Huh? Joke?

176
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:13,710
Of course it was.
Now, Climb <i>is</i> special, to be sure,

177
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:16,750
but he's special because he's <i>yours</i>.

178
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:17,960
Jeez...

179
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:23,220
Go on, feel free to sit down, Climb.
That nice tea will get cold.

180
00:12:25,430 --> 00:12:27,610
Let's go back to what
we were talking about before.

181
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:30,140
About Eight Fingers, right?

182
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:33,140
You're with me up to the part
where we burned the fields

183
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:36,230
that were growing the raw materials
for Black Dust, right?

184
00:12:36,230 --> 00:12:40,110
Yes. Lakyus, I really am grateful
to you and your team.

185
00:12:40,110 --> 00:12:43,430
My brother and the nobles do nothing
but quarrel among their factions,

186
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:47,120
and if they keep allowing Eight Fingers
to secretly do business

187
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:50,120
behind the scenes of the kingdom,
it will soon fall into ruin,

188
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:52,620
and the kingdom will 
collapse from the inside.

189
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:56,170
However, I do not have 
any influential backing,

190
00:12:56,170 --> 00:12:58,430
nor a military force at my discretion.

191
00:12:59,170 --> 00:13:02,630
Eight Fingers has ties to the nobles--
no, to the royals as well,

192
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:04,340
and if I'm to fight them,

193
00:13:04,340 --> 00:13:07,010
I have no choice but to turn
to adventurers, such as yourselves.

194
00:13:07,010 --> 00:13:10,260
Enough of that, now. We're friends, right?

195
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:13,620
Tina, let's have it.

196
00:13:16,310 --> 00:13:19,400
We discovered this at the village
where they were producing Black Dust.

197
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:20,750
Can you tell what it is?

198
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:23,400
This is a substitution cipher.

199
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:28,780
Makes sense. The reason 
this was left behind...

200
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:32,290
...was as a trap? Or for some other reason?

201
00:13:32,290 --> 00:13:35,140
If that were the case, they wouldn't
use something so hard. Mm-hmm.

202
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:40,420
If that's it, I have a hunch that
cracking this code will be pretty easy.

203
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:41,960
Unbelievable.

204
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:46,180
She says that she is powerless to help,

205
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:50,640
but I don't know anyone else
for whom the word "genius" is a better fit.

206
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:56,310
I cracked it. It isn't a written order,

207
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:59,390
but each one of these appear to be
the name of a village or building.

208
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,250
Seven of which are within the capital.

209
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:07,260
I wonder if these are Black Dust stockpiles,
or other critical sites.

210
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:10,620
I doubt they would have
anything that important written in code

211
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:13,200
and left in an ordinary production site.

212
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,450
It's probably bait.

213
00:14:15,830 --> 00:14:16,710
--Bait?
--Bait?

214
00:14:16,710 --> 00:14:21,340
Well, um, Eight Fingers is divided up
into eight different organizations, right?

215
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:25,300
Such as drugs, slave trafficking,
smuggling, and gambling.

216
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,970
Rumor has it that each section
has its own chief.

217
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:32,760
Then I believe these are the bases
for those other organizations.

218
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:36,730
Their goal is to temporarily
draw interest away from themselves.

219
00:14:36,730 --> 00:14:39,690
And they're using
their own partners as the bait?

220
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:43,480
That underground brothel isn't on here.

221
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:45,860
What is it?

222
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:49,200
Begging your pardon,
but thanks to Princess Renner's work,

223
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,370
I thought that such establishments
had been done away with.

224
00:14:51,370 --> 00:14:54,690
Yes, thanks to the slave 
trade being abolished.

225
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:58,080
However, there is still one
Eight Fingers underground brothel

226
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,880
in business in the capital.

227
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:05,630
Tell me, Renner, what would you say
to Blue Rose raiding the place?

228
00:15:06,170 --> 00:15:09,220
If we can turn up some evidence,
it would strike a powerful blow

229
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:12,260
against the nobles
who are in bed with Eight Fingers.

230
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:17,390
But that would create trouble
for your family, the Alveins.

231
00:15:17,390 --> 00:15:20,790
On the other hand, it would be
too much for Climb to handle alone.

232
00:15:21,690 --> 00:15:24,360
I am terribly sorry for my lack of strength.

233
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:26,400
Oh, I'm so sorry, Climb!

234
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:28,900
That isn't what I meant by that!

235
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:31,780
I rely on you most of all, Climb.

236
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:35,990
I know just how hard you work for me.

237
00:15:35,990 --> 00:15:38,410
Still, don't do anything too foolhardy, okay?

238
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:41,420
That isn't a request; it's an order.

239
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:45,170
If anything were to happen to you, I'd...

240
00:15:47,170 --> 00:15:50,920
Ahem... In any case,
while we can't ignore the brothel,

241
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,840
let's first discuss what we're going to do

242
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:55,130
about the other locations 
revealed by the code.

243
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:59,060
Right. We should take action quickly.

244
00:15:59,390 --> 00:16:02,450
They haven't realized that
we're the ones who attacked the village.

245
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:06,940
But they have to know that
this information has already gotten out.

246
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,820
Then is it okay if we borrow Climb from you?

247
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,820
I want him to go right away,

248
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:14,820
and tell Gagaran and the others
that we're going to be making our move.

249
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,650
Understood!

250
00:16:17,950 --> 00:16:20,910
Come to think of it,
Tina's investigation turned up the names

251
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:25,250
--Look. It sounds like the princess
is about to do something again.

252
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:25,250
--of several nobles who have dealings 
with the slave trade chief, Cocco Doll.

253
00:16:25,250 --> 00:16:27,500
It must be tough for those Blue Rose ladies.

254
00:16:28,210 --> 00:16:32,590
That nobleman's daughter
is currently serving as one of my maids.

255
00:16:32,590 --> 00:16:38,140
Huh? It doesn't seem likely
that she is here just to spy on you, but...

256
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:43,390
You're right. I'll have to
warn Climb to be careful.

257
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:53,570
Welcome... back... Lord Sebas...

258
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:57,830
I'm home, Tuare. I trust there were
no problems with your work?

259
00:16:57,830 --> 00:16:59,410
No... none...

260
00:16:59,410 --> 00:17:02,160
I see. Glad to hear it.

261
00:17:02,790 --> 00:17:05,170
What are we having for dinner today?

262
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:08,920
A stew... made with... potatoes...

263
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:13,300
I look forward to it.
Your cooking is tasty, Tuare.

264
00:17:14,090 --> 00:17:15,300
Oh... no...

265
00:17:16,050 --> 00:17:20,930
I mean it. Now, do you
have enough ingredients?

266
00:17:20,930 --> 00:17:24,060
Oh, I will... check later...

267
00:17:24,390 --> 00:17:26,310
Would you like to go shopping together?

268
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:30,060
No... that's... all right...

269
00:17:33,490 --> 00:17:36,820
Tuare, I understand why you are afraid.

270
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:39,950
You must be terrified of going outside.

271
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:44,710
But please rest at ease;
I, Sebas, will protect you.

272
00:17:44,710 --> 00:17:46,830
No matter what peril may befall you,

273
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:51,340
I will dash them all, and keep you safe.

274
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:54,510
Tuare, please step forward.

275
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:57,590
If you are scared,
I do not mind if you close your eyes.

276
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:02,350
Would you place your trust in me?

277
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:06,190
Lord Sebas, you are... a rascal...

278
00:18:06,190 --> 00:18:11,360
When you say it like that...
I cannot... say no...

279
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:16,450
Please do not worry.
I may not look it, but I am plenty strong.

280
00:18:16,450 --> 00:18:19,490
Indeed. There are only 41 others,

281
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:23,490
and perhaps a few more,
who are stronger than me.

282
00:18:23,490 --> 00:18:26,870
Is that... a lot...?

283
00:18:32,670 --> 00:18:35,010
My lady, I have returned.

284
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:37,470
Very good, Sebas.

285
00:18:44,770 --> 00:18:48,230
Are you sure we should not inform Lord Ains?

286
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:52,190
You must be in daily contact with him.

287
00:18:52,190 --> 00:18:55,730
Could you not simply make mention
of the woman when you speak to him?

288
00:18:55,730 --> 00:19:01,620
I have an extremely high regard
for her culinary abilities. Moreover,

289
00:19:01,620 --> 00:19:05,290
it might be seen as odd for only two people

290
00:19:05,290 --> 00:19:08,910
to be living in such a large mansion
as this, might it not?

291
00:19:08,910 --> 00:19:11,630
You are saying that this is
part of a diversionary tactic?

292
00:19:11,630 --> 00:19:16,420
Correct. If I seek permission from
Lord Ains over maintaining our cover,

293
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:19,880
he will snap at me, and tell me
to think for myself over such a thing.

294
00:19:23,970 --> 00:19:29,270
I am Staffan Havish, a constable
charged with keeping the capital safe.

295
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:31,520
So, what can I do for you?

296
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:34,900
There is an establishment--
well, <i>his</i> establishment, as it happens...

297
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:38,400
Succulent. It is a pleasure to meet you.

298
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:41,450
I received a report from
his establishment, you see,

299
00:19:41,450 --> 00:19:45,450
that someone carrying a scroll
bearing the seal of the magicians' guild

300
00:19:45,450 --> 00:19:47,330
handed over an inordinate amount of money

301
00:19:47,330 --> 00:19:50,410
and carried off one of
the establishment's employees.

302
00:19:50,410 --> 00:19:54,250
Slave trafficking is prohibited
within the kingdom,

303
00:19:54,250 --> 00:19:58,840
and it sounds as though
this was a violation of that.

304
00:19:58,840 --> 00:19:59,840
Is that so?

305
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:00,760
Huh?

306
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:03,970
I will let my butler, Sebas,
deal with this touchy matter.

307
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:07,970
Sebas, you handle it from here.
Good day, gentlemen.

308
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:12,270
Now then, in my lady's stead,

309
00:20:12,270 --> 00:20:16,520
I will hear whatever it is you have to say.

310
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,610
Well, from the circumstantial evidence,

311
00:20:19,610 --> 00:20:23,030
it is beyond a doubt
that you have committed a crime,

312
00:20:23,030 --> 00:20:27,490
but the establishment
is willing to offer you clemency.

313
00:20:27,490 --> 00:20:32,080
Naturally, this will incur
consolation payments and commissions.

314
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:34,710
I see. How much will that cost?

315
00:20:34,710 --> 00:20:37,170
It will be 500 gold coins.

316
00:20:37,170 --> 00:20:42,800
That is extortionate. She 
was in a terrible state.

317
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:46,050
If you were to take her away now,
she might very well die.

318
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:48,310
You don't say, you don't say.

319
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:51,310
Well then, until she is done convalescing,

320
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:55,730
what would you say to loaning us
the lady of your house?

321
00:20:55,730 --> 00:20:59,190
Oh, indeed, your lost income
must be compensated.

322
00:20:59,190 --> 00:21:01,740
Is your excessive lust not a problem for you?

323
00:21:02,070 --> 00:21:05,110
Huh?! How rude of you to mention lust!

324
00:21:05,110 --> 00:21:09,700
This whole law originally
came about at the noble behest

325
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:12,200
of the eminent Golden Princess, Renner!
You dare to--

326
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:15,790
Now, now, please calm yourself, Lord Havish.

327
00:21:15,790 --> 00:21:18,590
We will return for your decision
the day after tomorrow.

328
00:21:18,590 --> 00:21:20,750
Will that be all right, Mr. Sebas?

329
00:21:21,670 --> 00:21:23,440
Understood.

330
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:31,310
What are you going to do?

331
00:21:31,310 --> 00:21:35,060
I think I would like to think this through
over a short stroll outside.

332
00:21:42,150 --> 00:21:43,270
Message.

333
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,610
Is that you, Lord Ains?

334
00:21:47,610 --> 00:21:51,080
Solution? I'm surprised 
to have you contact me.

335
00:21:51,490 --> 00:21:52,870
Is there an emergency?

336
00:21:52,870 --> 00:21:56,210
Yes. There is a chance
that Lord Sebas has turned on us.

337
00:21:56,580 --> 00:21:59,250
Hmm. Huh? Eh?! You can't mean it!

338
00:21:59,250 --> 00:22:02,130
Ahem, no more kidding around, Solution.

339
00:22:02,130 --> 00:22:05,970
A declaration like that without
any proof cannot go unanswered.

340
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:08,220
Is there any?

341
00:22:08,220 --> 00:22:09,130
Yes.

342
00:22:09,130 --> 00:22:11,130


